:R-HSA-444473  a            obo:GO_0008150 , owl:NamedIndividual ;
        rdfs:comment        "The formyl peptide receptor (FPR) was defined pharmacologically in 1976 as a high affinity binding site on the surface of neutrophils for the peptide N-formyl-methionine-leucine-phenylalanine (fMLF). FPR was cloned in 1990 and the cDNA used as a probe to identify two additional genes, FPRL1 and FPRL2. The three genes for a cluster on 19q13.3. All are coupled to the Gi family of G proteins. <br> All 3 receptors can be activated by formyl peptides but also display affinities for a range of structurally diverse ligands." ;
        rdfs:label          "Formyl peptide receptors bind formyl peptides and many other ligands" ;
        dc:contributor      "Authored: Jupe, S, 2009-10-22" , "Reviewed: D'Eustachio, P, 2009-12-11" , "Edited: Jupe, S, 2010-03-01" , "GOC:reactome_curators" ;
        dc:date             "2023-06-21" ;
        pav:providedBy      "https://reactome.org" ;
        oboInOwl:hasDbXref  "R-HSA-444473" ;
        skos:narrower       <http://model.geneontology.org/R-HSA-375276/R-HSA-375276> ;
        skos:note           "org.biopax.paxtools.model.level3.Pathway" .

